{% render 'section-style', section: section %}
{%- comment -%}
  How it's made — the process animation.

  Built from Aaron's "Process animation sequence.zip" export, deliberately NOT
  rebuilt from scratch: the artwork, the timing and the copy are the designed
  work and are carried across unchanged.

  FOUR sanctioned changes, all approved 2026-08-03, nothing else touched:

  1. Accents now match the drink. The six originals were replaced with colours
     sampled off the product photography — the median of the liquid band on
     each bottle shot — lifted only far enough to clear 3:1 on the near-black
     ground. NON9 is the one departure: in glass it photographs identically to
     NON7, so its hue was moved to plum, which is what Oaked Blackberry & Plum
     actually is.
  2. Colour is on the DRAWINGS only. The selector chips and the step label
     used the accent too; they are monochrome now. Aaron's ruling was that the
     fruit may have colour, not the interface.
  3. Fonts mapped to the house stack — the mono and sans custom properties in
     place of SF Mono and Helvetica Neue.
  4. React is NOT hot-linked. support.js is vendored into the theme as
     dc-support.js so the page carries no third-party runtime dependency.

  The artifact is wrapped in a raw block below. Its templating uses double
  braces, which is Liquid's own syntax — unwrapped, Shopify consumes all 87
  placeholders and the animation renders blank.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="non-process-anim">
  {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank or section.settings.heading != blank -%}
    <div class="non-process-anim__head">
      {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <div class="non-mono non-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
        <h2 class="non-process-anim__title">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="non-process-anim__stage">
    {% render 'process-anim-1' %}
    {% render 'process-anim-2' %}
    {% render 'process-anim-3' %}
    {% render 'process-anim-4' %}

  </div>
</div>

{%- comment -%}
  React and ReactDOM served from the THEME, not unpkg.

  dc-support's loadReactUmd() short-circuits on `if (w.React && w.ReactDOM)`,
  so loading them first from our own assets means it never reaches its CDN
  branch and the page carries no third-party runtime dependency. No patching
  of the vendored runtime required — it simply finds React already there.

  defer preserves document order, so React is guaranteed to be defined before
  dc-support runs. Babel is never fetched: the artifact's script contains no
  JSX, so that branch is dead here and its 2.5MB never loads.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script src="{{ 'vendor-react.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
<script src="{{ 'vendor-react-dom.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
<script src="{{ 'dc-support.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Process animation",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "How it's made" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Appearance" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "bg_color", "label": "Background" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "section_padding", "label": "Vertical padding", "min": 0, "max": 160, "step": 8, "unit": "px", "default": 0, "info": "0 keeps the section's own spacing." }
  ],
  "presets": [ { "name": "Process animation" } ]
}
{% endschema %}
